<title>AUSTRIA: VA Tech unit wins 320 mln ATS rail order.</title>
<headline>VA Tech unit wins 320 mln ATS rail order.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elin Antriebstechnik, a unit of Austria's VA Technologie, said on Wednesday it had won a 320 million schillings order to provide equipment for railcars by Talbot, a German subsidiary of Canada's Bombardier.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the electrical equipment would be used by German railway operator Deutsche Bahn AG in new rail vehicles in suburban and regional transport, primarily on non-electrified track sections.</p>
<p>Delivery of the first vehicles was scheduled for the beginning of next year, it added.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
